_kind\">constructor</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.PolyDerivation.step\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">CommRing</span>.<span class=\"name\">PolyDerivation</span>.<span class=\"name\">step</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">p</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k₁</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">d</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.PolyDerivation\">PolyDerivation</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k₂</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">m₂</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Mon\">Mon</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.EqCnstr\">EqCnstr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.PolyDerivation\">PolyDerivation</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"```\np = k₁*d.p + k₂*m₂*c.p\n```\nThe coefficient `k₁` is used because the leading monomial in `c` may not be monic.\nThus, if we follow the chain back to the input polynomial, we have that\n`p = C * input_p` for a `C` that is equal to the product of all `k₁`s in the chain.\n`C ≠ 1` can happen in any ring, but `C` can be cancelled only if the ring implements\n`NoNatZeroDivisors`. That is, `p = 0` implies `input_p = 0` only if `C = 1` or the ring\nimplements `NoNatZeroDivisors`. Simplifying with `checkCoeffDvd := true` guarantees\n`C = 1` in rings without `NoNatZeroDivisors`, see `Mon.findSimp?`.\nHere is a small example where we simplify `x+y` using the equations\n`2*x - 1 = 0` (`c₁`), `3*y - 1 = 0` (`c₂`), and `6*z + 5 = 0` (`c₃`)\n```\nx + y + z            | s₁ := .input (x + y + z)\n*2\n=   - 1*1*(2*x - 1)\n2*y + 2*z + 1        | s₂ := .step (2*y + 2*z + 1) 2 s₁ (-1) 1 c₁\n*3\n=   - 2*1*(3*y - 1)\n6*z + 5              | s₃ := .step (6*z + 5) 3 s₂ (-2) 1 c₂\n=   - 1*1*(6*z + 5)\n0                    | s₄ := .step (0) 1 s₃ (-1) 1 c₃\n```\nFor this chain, we build the certificate\n```\n(-3)*(2*x - 1) + (-2)*(3*y - 1) + (-1)*(6*z + 5)\n```\nfor\n```\n0 = 6*(x + y + z)\n```\nRecall that if the ring implement `NoNatZeroDivisors`, then the following property holds:\n```\n∀ (k : Int) (a : α), k ≠ 0 → (intCast k) * a = 0 → a = 0\n```\ngrind can deduce that `x+y+z = 0`","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.PolyDerivation.step","kind":"ctor","line":87,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.PolyDerivation.step","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.lean#L87-L125"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">constructor</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.PolyDerivation.input\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">CommRing</span>.<span class=\"name\">PolyDerivation</span>.<span class=\"name\">input</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">p</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.PolyDerivation\">PolyDerivation</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.PolyDerivation.input","kind":"ctor","line":86,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.PolyDerivation.input","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.lean#L86-L86"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">inductive</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.PolyDerivation\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">CommRing</span>.<span class=\"name\">PolyDerivation</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"A polynomial `p` equipped with a chain of rewrite steps that justifies `p = C * input`, where\n`input` is the original polynomial and `C` is the product of the multipliers `k₁` of the\n`.step`s in the chain (`C = 1` when every step is monic). `C ≠ 1` is possible in any ring,\nincluding those with `NoNatZeroDivisors`; the instance only lets `C` be cancelled.\nFrom an input polynomial, we use equations (i.e., `EqCnstr`) as rewriting rules.\nFor example, consider the following sequence of rewrites for the input polynomial `2*x^2 + x*y`\nusing the equations `x - 1 = 0` (`c₁`) and `y - 2 = 0` (`c₂`).\n```\n2*x^2 + x*y                  | s₁ := .input (2*x^2 + x*y)\n=           - 2*x*(x - 1)\n(2*x + x*y)                  | s₂ := .step (2*x + x*y)  1 s₁ (-2) x c₁\n=           - 2*1*(x - 1)\n(x*y + 2)                    | s₃ := .step (x*y + 2) 1 s₂ (-2) 1 c₁\n=           - 1*y*(x - 1)\n(y + 2)                      | s₄ := .step (y+2) 1 s₃ (-1) y c₁\n=           - 1*1*(y - 2)\n4                            | s₅ := .step 4 1 s₄ (-1) 1 c₂\n```\nFrom the chain above, we build the certificate\n```\n(-2*x - y - 2)*(x-1) + (-1)*(y-2)\n```\nfor\n```\n4 = (2*x^2 + x*y)\n```\nbecause `x-1 = 0` and `y-2=0`","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.PolyDerivation","kind":"inductive","line":56,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.PolyDerivation","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.lean#L56-L132"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">abbrev</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.Queue\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">CommRing</span>.<span class=\"name\">Queue</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.Queue","kind":"def","line":54,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.Queue","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.lean#L54-L54"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.EqCnstr.compare\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">CommRing</span>.<span class=\"name\">EqCnstr</span>.<span class=\"name\">compare</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c₁ </span><span class=\"fn\">c₂</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.EqCnstr\">EqCnstr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Ord/Basic.html#Ordering\">Ordering</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.EqCnstr.compare","kind":"def","line":49,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.EqCnstr.compare","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.lean#L49-L52"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">instance</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.instInhabitedEqCnstr\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">CommRing</span>.<span class=\"name\">instInhabitedEqCnstr</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Inhabited\">Inhabited</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.EqCnstr\">EqCnstr</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/CommRing/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.instInhabitedEqCnstr","kind":"instance","line":46,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.CommRing.instInhabitedEqCnstr","sourceLink":"https://github.